@startuml Resource_Management_SSD
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.12 “Register and Manage Physical Resources”

' Participants – architectural layers
actor "Logistics Operator" as Operator
boundary "ResourcesController\n(API Layer)" as Controller
control "ResourceService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "ResourceMapper\n(Data Mapper)" as Mapper
entity "Resource\n(Domain Entity)" as Resource
collections "IResourceRepository / ResourceRepository\n(Persistence)" as Repo
database "Azure SQL Database\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

' Contextual Note
note over Operator
User Story 2.2.12
--------------------------------
"As a Logistics Operator, I want to
register and manage physical resources
(create, update, deactivate),
so that they can be considered
during planning and scheduling."
end note

== 1. Create Resource ==
Operator -> Controller: POST /api/resources (ResourceDTO)
activate Controller

Controller -> Mapper: ToDomain(ResourceDTO)
activate Mapper
Mapper --> Controller: Resource (Domain Entity)
deactivate Mapper

Controller -> Service: RegisterResourceAsync(Resource)
activate Service

Service -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(Resource.Id)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: null (no duplicate found)
deactivate Repo

note over Service
Validation:
- Ensure unique alphanumeric Code
- Validate Description, Capacity, SetupTime
- Verify Qualification requirements exist
end note

Service -> Repo: AddAsync(Resource)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: INSERT INTO Resources(...)
activate DB
DB --> Repo: Success
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Resource persisted
deactivate Repo

Service --> Controller: Created Resource
deactivate Service
Controller --> Operator: 201 Created + ResourceDTO
deactivate Controller

== 2. Update Resource ==
Operator -> Controller: PUT /api/resources/{id}
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: UpdateResourceAsync(Resource)
activate Service

Service -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: Existing Resource
deactivate Repo

Service -> Resource: Apply new description, setupTime, capacity
note over Resource
Domain logic:
- Validate new values
- Keep previous version for audit
end note
Service -> Repo: SaveChangesAsync(Resource)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: UPDATE Resources SET ...
activate DB
DB --> Repo: OK
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Updated Resource
deactivate Repo
Service --> Controller: 204 No Content
Controller --> Operator: Confirmation (Resource updated)
deactivate Controller
deactivate Service

== 3. Deactivate Resource ==
Operator -> Controller: PATCH /api/resources/{id}/deactivate
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: DeactivateAsync(id)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: Resource found (Status=Active)
deactivate Repo

note over Service
Business rule:
Only Active or UnderMaintenance
resources can be deactivated.
end note

Service -> Resource: Change status to Inactive
Service -> Repo: UpdateAvailabilityAsync(id, Inactive)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: UPDATE Resources SET Status='Inactive'
activate DB
DB --> Repo: OK
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Updated Resource
deactivate Repo
Service --> Controller: ResourceDTO (Inactive)
Controller --> Operator: 200 OK (Resource Deactivated)
deactivate Controller
deactivate Service

== 4. Search & Filter ==
Operator -> Controller: GET /api/resources?status=Active&type=Truck
activate Controller
Controller -> Service: GetAllResourcesAsync()
activate Service
Service -> Repo: GetAllAsync()
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM Resources
activate DB
DB --> Repo: List<Resource>
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Resources
Service -> Controller: Filtered Resources (by status, type)
Controller --> Operator: 200 OK + JSON[List<ResourceDTO>]
deactivate Controller
deactivate Service

@enduml
